{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/328644-fae-plot-for-a-werewolf-game","id":328644,"title":"Fae Plot for a Werewolf game:","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-02T14:59:24-08:00","id":328644,"title":"Fae Plot for a Werewolf game:","content":"I plan on doing something endangering the veil with some Fae. I was thinking of perhaps cursing a human with a curse of lycanthropcy that thanks to genuine werewolf existence doesn't quite get covered up by the mists properly. How absurd is this with changeling? Or is it possible at all? I like to stick as close as possible to the canon rules and themes of the other genre's.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/494-exalted-viovode","name":"Exalted Viovode","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T19:55:33-08:00","id":328849,"title":"","content":"Its a interesting concept. If the Changeling rules allow it then go for it, if not story trumps rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-03T05:37:38-08:00","id":329138,"title":"","content":"I think it would do the Dreaming a disservice to believe there wasn't a place where lycanthropy is a disease and not a heriditary trait. Your real challenge would be figuring out what sort of Sidhe sorcerer, or perhaps Tuatha, actually has the power to drag that disease into the real world and enchant a mortal into believing they have it. That's powerful glamour, and the host has to be very carefully selected to avoid them unweaving the spell with banality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4297-explodingjoe","name":"ExplodingJoe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4297_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-03T06:25:55-08:00","id":329159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ExplodingJoe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/328644-fae-plot-for-a-werewolf-game?p=329138#post329138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it would do the Dreaming a disservice to believe there wasn't a place where lycanthropy is a disease and not a heriditary trait. Your real challenge would be figuring out what sort of Sidhe sorcerer, or perhaps Tuatha, actually has the power to drag that disease into the real world and enchant a mortal into believing they have it. That's powerful glamour, and the host has to be very carefully selected to avoid them unweaving the spell with banality.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, the real challenge will be finding ways that werewolves can actually deal with the problem. I've never seen changeling/werewolf crossover work out well for anything other than the occasional pagan celebration/orgy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-03T17:58:08-08:00","id":329693,"title":"","content":"My game's pack has a new Fianna I want to torture by giving fae blood (I love turning merits into flaws), I plan on making her intrinsic to actually finding the source of the contagion... maybe a wolfish Pooka has been cursed by an upper level Sidhe? My knowledge of changeling is limited, so any help with defining the antagonist I'm looking to use is appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/494-exalted-viovode","name":"Exalted Viovode","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-03T20:11:30-08:00","id":329829,"title":"","content":"I'm almost positive you could do so with the art Naming. So any sufficiently skilled Sidhe (generally the only ones with it) with max levels of the art should be able to do so. I don't have my books here, but I seem to remember Naming basically being able to do whatever you want with sufficient successes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T12:53:40-08:00","id":330474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/328644-fae-plot-for-a-werewolf-game?p=329159#post329159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, the real challenge will be finding ways that werewolves can actually deal with the problem. I've never seen changeling/werewolf crossover work out well for anything other than the occasional pagan celebration/orgy.</div> </div> </div> </div>The easiest is usually that a particular trod is a site of great gnosis, which they tend to be anyway. Arcadia is a realm of the Umbra. Garou and Fae band together to protect the place. True - it's a challenging sell if none of the Garou are Fianna.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exalted Viovode</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">maybe a wolfish Pooka has been cursed by an upper level Sidhe? My knowledge of changeling is limited, so any help with defining the antagonist I'm looking to use is appreciated.</div> </div> </div> </div>The art you'd be looking for is called Metamorphosis. At 5th level, a Fae sorcerer can transform someone into a beast of legend, of which I would say Werewolves are in the deluded mortal mindset. A decent hook might be that this sorcerer is of the Shadow Court and intent on destroying the workings of the local fae. If a Sidhe is doing this to common folk like Pooka, there's also the risk of inciting another commoner riot among the nearby fae courts.<br /> <br /> The biggest issue is that anyone altered with Metamorphosis 5 is in danger of being ejected straight into the Dreaming if struck by banality. Garou aren't the most banal creatures, but mortals certainly are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4297-explodingjoe","name":"ExplodingJoe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4297_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T13:33:31-08:00","id":330508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ExplodingJoe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/328644-fae-plot-for-a-werewolf-game?p=330474#post330474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The easiest is usually that a particular trod is a site of great gnosis, which they tend to be anyway. Arcadia is a realm of the Umbra. Garou and Fae band together to protect the place. True - it's a challenging sell if none of the Garou are Fianna.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Arcadian Gateway isn't supposed to actually be connected to the Arcadia changelings refer to. In W20 they've changed it a bit, making it more Fae friendly.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ExplodingJoe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/328644-fae-plot-for-a-werewolf-game?p=330474#post330474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The art you'd be looking for is called Metamorphosis. At 5th level, a Fae sorcerer can transform someone into a beast of legend, of which I would say Werewolves are in the deluded mortal mindset. A decent hook might be that this sorcerer is of the Shadow Court and intent on destroying the workings of the local fae. If a Sidhe is doing this to common folk like Pooka, there's also the risk of inciting another commoner riot among the nearby fae courts.<br /> <br /> The biggest issue is that anyone altered with Metamorphosis 5 is in danger of being ejected straight into the Dreaming if struck by banality. Garou aren't the most banal creatures, but mortals certainly are.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking that through some quirk of the mists react with the delierium causing the effect to be sustained and quasi banality resistant. Since humans all have an instinctual fear and knowledge of werewolves at a subconscious level, their conscious disbelief is undermined by their hereditary nightmares of the Imperium<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/494-exalted-viovode","name":"Exalted Viovode","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T13:55:32-08:00","id":330517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exalted Viovode</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/328644-fae-plot-for-a-werewolf-game?p=330508#post330508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was thinking that through some quirk of the mists react with the delierium causing the effect to be sustained and quasi banality resistant. Since humans all have an instinctual fear and knowledge of werewolves at a subconscious level, their conscious disbelief is undermined by their hereditary nightmares of the Imperium</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a fairly creative way of tackling it, and I'd give it a pass. The price for Metamorphosis 5 is a permanent point of glamour, so this is end game for whatever insideous mind is behind the spell.<br /> <br /> If you want some heads up about the art for the sake of the villain's power - Metamorphosis one is like Veiled Eyes, but works through camoflauge rather than jedi mind tricks. Two dots allows you to look like other people. Three dots is &quot;Go Ask Alice&quot; and allows you to change the size of things. Four dots allows you to shapeshift people into animals Merlin's lessons for Arthur style. 5 dots is the afformentioned.<br /> <br /> Any fae can/will learn this art, though it's origin was among the common folk. Also, I forgot where I read it, but most Werewolves are considered to have rather low banality (like Grump level) as most tribes still have ancestor spirits who remember fighting against or alongside fae. The Get and Fianna more than others. If you have a Get in your pack - their elders swore a blood oath to murder the Sidhe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4297-explodingjoe","name":"ExplodingJoe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4297_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T16:09:22-08:00","id":330584,"title":"","content":"The Get swore an oath to murder the Sidhe?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/494-exalted-viovode","name":"Exalted Viovode","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T18:47:44-08:00","id":330698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exalted Viovode</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/328644-fae-plot-for-a-werewolf-game?p=330584#post330584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Get swore an oath to murder the Sidhe?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's addressed in the Changeling storyteller's guide. This is from memory, so I might be off on the details, but the gist of it is: Once upon a time, a group of Sidhe got lost in the woods and their horses were killed. They spotted a pack of Dire wolves and decided they would make fine steeds. They used their magic to enslave the pack and force them into service as mounts. The pack was a pack of Get of Fenris. Some time later, they were released (I think) and word spread and ever since, the Get have a sworn oath against the Sidhe to kill them on sight.<br /> I don't recall anything about this story though, from the Get point of view (Werewolf books) but it is an interesting bit of lore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T07:27:34-08:00","id":331060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ExplodingJoe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/328644-fae-plot-for-a-werewolf-game?p=330474#post330474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The easiest is usually that a particular trod is a site of great gnosis, which they tend to be anyway. Arcadia is a realm of the Umbra. Garou and Fae band together to protect the place. True - it's a challenging sell if none of the Garou are Fianna.</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant that Werewolf players are rarely familiar with Changeling mechanics and even if they are, their characters are usually completely unable to deal with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T07:34:45-08:00","id":331065,"title":"","content":"Basically, what idpersona said. The Sidhe come across a Troll and a Get fighting over who's stronger. After the fight is over, the Get runs off using the his snow walking gift. The Sidhe are so impressed by the wolf's ability to move across the tundra that they track down his pack and enchant them all to be slaves and mounts. Later the Get break free of the slavery, and relate the tale to the rest of the tribe. Most Fenrir don't need much more reason to declare war, so it's decided that the Fenrir will pay back the Aelfar with blood. Of course, most Get these days probly don't know fairies exist, unless they've been raised in the wilds of northern Scandinavia. You can realistically expect to have been raised on tales of fae lore if you grew up in rural Ireland, Scandinavia or Finland.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4297-explodingjoe","name":"ExplodingJoe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4297_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-06T05:00:27-08:00","id":332152,"title":"","content":"If interested in playing with the Sidhe/Get idea, then any Get with Ancestors background could also be informed immediately. That's how I went about it in my game. For that matter, any spirits that serve Fenris can pass along the message as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-06T14:37:08-08:00","id":332506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/328644-fae-plot-for-a-werewolf-game?p=330698#post330698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's addressed in the Changeling storyteller's guide. This is from memory, so I might be off on the details, but the gist of it is: Once upon a time, a group of Sidhe got lost in the woods and their horses were killed. They spotted a pack of Dire wolves and decided they would make fine steeds. They used their magic to enslave the pack and force them into service as mounts. The pack was a pack of Get of Fenris. Some time later, they were released (I think) and word spread and ever since, the Get have a sworn oath against the Sidhe to kill them on sight.<br /> I don't recall anything about this story though, from the Get point of view (Werewolf books) but it is an interesting bit of lore.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Get of Fenris point of view from the Revised Tribebook is &quot;Alfar? Don't know anything about them. Next question.&quot; The story is never related by werewolves, as if the game never had time to entertain any details from Changeling books that no one was apparently expected to read.<br /> <br /> (Also really wishing that WW people did more/actual research on dire wolves back in the day.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-06T21:03:08-08:00","id":332731,"title":"","content":"Well to be fair both the Get and the Spirits themselves are just as susceptible to the Mists as everyone else so even if the Sidhe had used them as their rides in the past the mists would have hidden that fact from the wolves a long time ago.<br /> <br /> So you can either use it or leave it as suits you but in both cases the truth should be rather obfuscated due to the Mists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-07T19:14:14-08:00","id":333677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/328644-fae-plot-for-a-werewolf-game?p=332731#post332731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well to be fair both the Get and the Spirits themselves are just as susceptible to the Mists as everyone else so even if the Sidhe had used them as their rides in the past the mists would have hidden that fact from the wolves a long time ago.<br /> <br /> So you can either use it or leave it as suits you but in both cases the truth should be rather obfuscated due to the Mists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough point. Interestingly, I had never considered that the Mists would work on spirits. The thought just never occurred to me, I kind of assumed they would have some sort of immunity, being not of this world. /Shrug","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T06:31:38-08:00","id":334161,"title":"","content":"Well, as I recall, Tribebook Get came out in 1993, and Changeling's 1st ed wasn't until 1995. Being the redheaded stepchild of World of Darkness, I never really expected Changeling would be integrated closely into the other books. I mean, most books taught you how to make fae using vampire disciplines or werewolf gifts. I always found that hilarious. Imagine a Sidhe throwing out Presence and Dominate at mortals as if it were Protocol.<br /> <br /> More to the point though. If you have any issues with the history from Changeling not jiving with the history from Werewolf, Changeling STs always have a way out - the mists did it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4297-explodingjoe","name":"ExplodingJoe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4297_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T07:50:40-08:00","id":334202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ExplodingJoe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/328644-fae-plot-for-a-werewolf-game?p=334161#post334161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, as I recall, Tribebook Get came out in 1993, and Changeling's 1st ed wasn't until 1995. Being the redheaded stepchild of World of Darkness, I never really expected Changeling would be integrated closely into the other books. I mean, most books taught you how to make fae using vampire disciplines or werewolf gifts. I always found that hilarious. Imagine a Sidhe throwing out Presence and Dominate at mortals as if it were Protocol.<br /> <br /> More to the point though. If you have any issues with the history from Changeling not jiving with the history from Werewolf, Changeling STs always have a way out - the mists did it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, the first (and awful) GoF Tribebook came out after the second edition did, which would place it after 1994. There was ample opportunity to address it in the later, much better tribebook of Revised vintage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T11:19:19-08:00","id":334367,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I figured my head timeline would be inaccurate. Damn million updated and revised everythings. I'm going to stick with my assertion that the mists kept it from anyone who wasn't connected to specific ancestor spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4297-explodingjoe","name":"ExplodingJoe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4297_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T19:22:34-08:00","id":334734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exalted Viovode</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/328644-fae-plot-for-a-werewolf-game?p=330584#post330584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Get swore an oath to murder the Sidhe?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This was a very bad idea casually dropped in a late edition Changeling supplement. No consideration was given that for many years, players likely had Get of Fenris PCs in packs with Stag as a totem (bound to help Fae) that this &quot;blood oath&quot; would completely screw up. In my chronicles, I limit it to a single Sidhe House and tied it into the actual legend of the binding of Fenris Wolf. I basically said that the Vanir were a Sidhe House. This combined with Odin being a Gangrel Methusaleh effectively explains why Norse legend records Fenris destroying the &quot;gods&quot; while not actually making Fenris part of the Wyrm host during Ragnarok.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T21:00:48-08:00","id":334797,"title":"","content":"Nicely fit in. It only ever came up for me in 1 chronicle, and the pack totem was Grandfather Thunder, so there was no conflict of interest. I could absolutely see how this would've been an issue if it was Stag though. it can be frustrating when crossover information contradicts itself like that, which I think is part of why so many people are against it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-09T07:51:00-08:00","id":335185,"title":"","content":"Fenrir following Stag, huh? I guess the Fianna really did win the war.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4297-explodingjoe","name":"ExplodingJoe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4297_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-09T12:14:50-08:00","id":335369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ExplodingJoe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/328644-fae-plot-for-a-werewolf-game?p=335185#post335185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fenrir following Stag, huh? I guess the Fianna really did win the war.</div> </div> </div> </div>It hinges on no one talking about it. Just walk away and let the Fenrir spend time hanging out with the giants, and everything will be alright.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T00:54:34-08:00","id":339817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/328644-fae-plot-for-a-werewolf-game?p=334797#post334797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nicely fit in. It only ever came up for me in 1 chronicle, and the pack totem was Grandfather Thunder, so there was no conflict of interest. I could absolutely see how this would've been an issue if it was Stag though. it can be frustrating when crossover information contradicts itself like that, which I think is part of why so many people are against it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always assume the idiosyncrasies are the result of the telephone game in a world where all conspiracies are true, even the one's that contradict.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cIt was clear to me for a long time that the origins of science had their deep roots in a particular myth, that of invariance.&quot; ~ Giorgio de Santillana<br /> Preface to Hamlet's Mill","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","name":"Whithers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2345_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[